"Methods: IPCC inventory methodologies","slug":"method_ipcc","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64341,64344,64325],"labels":{"1284639":{"name":"IPCC 1996 Guidelines","slug":null,"index":1},"1284640":{"name":"IPCC 2006 Guidelines","slug":null,"index":2},"1284641":{"name":"IPCC 2019 Guidelines","slug":null,"index":3},"1284642":{"name":"Not Specified","slug":null,"index":4},"1284643":{"name":"Multiple IPCC Guidelines","slug":null,"index":5},"1284644":{"name":"Non-specific IPCC Guidelines","slug":null,"index":6},"1284645":{"name":"No Document Submitted","slug":null,"index":-2}},"locations":{"IDN":[{"value":"\"Emission in reference year is estimated emission from the GHG Inventory using 2006 IPCC-GL.\"","label_id":1284640,"document_slug":"second_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified","label_id":1284642,"document_slug":"revised_first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not specified","label_id":1284642,"document_slug":"first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Inventory is based on 2006 IPCC Guidelines for National Greenhouse Gas inventories and the IPCC GHG for LULUCF.\u003cbr\u003eAll data will refer to the National Inventory System of Greenhouse Gases (SIGN SMART), UNFCCC Biennial Update Report (BUR), and FREL-REDD+ document.","label_id":1284640,"document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648510,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"Methods: Global warming potential (GWP) values","slug":"method_gwp","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64341,64344,64325],"labels":{"1284646":{"name":"AR2 GWP values","slug":null,"index":1},"1284647":{"name":"AR3 GWP values","slug":null,"index":2},"1284648":{"name":"AR4 GWP values","slug":null,"index":3},"1284649":{"name":"AR5 GWP values","slug":null,"index":4},"1284650":{"name":"AR6 GWP values","slug":null,"index":5},"1284651":{"name":"Not Specified","slug":null,"index":6},"1284652":{"name":"No Document Submitted","slug":null,"index":-2}},"locations":{"IDN":[{"value":"\"Global Warming Potential (GWP) on a 100-year timescale in accordance with the IPCC’s 5th Assessment Report.\"","label_id":1284649,"document_slug":"second_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"\"Global Warming Potential (GWP) on a 100-year timescale in accordance with the IPCC’s 2nd Assessment Report.\"","label_id":1284646,"document_slug":"revised_first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Global Warming Potential (GWP) on a 100 year timescale in accordance with the IPCC's 4th Assessment Report.","label_id":1284648,"document_slug":"first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Global Warming Potential (GWP) on a 100 year timescale in accordance with the IPCC's 4th Assessment Report.","label_id":1284648,"document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648511,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"Baseline scenario targets: Static or dynamic baseline scenario","slug":"method_baseline_static_dynamic","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64341,64344],"labels":{},"locations":{"IDN":[{"value":"Not Specified","document_slug":"revised_first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified","document_slug":"first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified","document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648512,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"Baseline scenario targets: Cut-off year for policies included in the baseline scenario, and any significant policies excluded from the baseline scenario","slug":"method_baseline_year","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64341,64344],"labels":{},"locations":{"IDN":[{"value":"\"BAU scenarios of emission projection started in 2010.\"","document_slug":"revised_first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"BAU scenarios of emission projection started in 2010.","document_slug":"first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified","document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648513,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"Baseline scenario targets: Projection method","slug":"method_baseline_projection_method","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64341,64344],"labels":{},"locations":{"IDN":[{"value":"\"Model for estimating emission: Dashboard AFOLU for land-based sector; ExSS (Extended Snapshot) using GAMS (General Algebraic Modelling System) and CGE (Dynamic CGE) for energy sector; Mitigation Action Road Map for Cement Industry (Ministry of Industry) for IPPU sector; First Order Decay-FOD (IPCC-2006) and existing regulation for waste sector.\"","document_slug":"revised_first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMethodology for Estimating Emissions\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eModel for estimating emission:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eDashboard AFOLU for land-based sector;\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eExSS (\u003cem\u003eExtended Snap Shot\u003c/em\u003e) using GAMS (\u003cem\u003eGeneral Algebraic Modeling System\u003c/em\u003e) and CGE (Dynamic CGE) for energy sector;\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eMitigation Action Road Map for Cement Industry (Ministry of Industry) for IPPU sector;\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cem\u003eFirst Order Decay\u003c/em\u003e-FOD (IPCC-2006) and existing regulation for waste sector\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBaseline, Assumption Used for Projection and Policy Scenario 2020-2030\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eBAU Baseline Scenario and Mitigation Scenario\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eBAU Scenario: emission scenario when the development path does not consider the mitigation policies.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eCounter Measure 1 Scenario (CM1): emission scenario with mitigation scenario and considers sectoral development target.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eCounter Measure 2 Scenario (CM2) or conditional scenario: emission scenario with more ambitious mitigation scenario and considers sectoral development target when international support is available.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","document_slug":"first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"BAU scenarios of emission projection started in 2010, with each sector having various data year interval. For example, the historical data of land-based sector is available from 1990-2012, as seen in Indonesian FREL-REDD+ submission.","document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648514,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"Baseline scenario targets: Emission drivers included and assumptions and data sources for key drivers","slug":"method_baseline_emission_drivers","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64341,64344],"labels":{},"locations":{"IDN":[{"value":"Please refer to the Annex 1 of the NDC for assumptions used for projected BAU and emission reduction (unconditional/CM1 and conditional/ CM2 reduction) for all sector categories (Energy, Waste, IPPU, Agriculture, and Forestry)","document_slug":"revised_first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Please refer to the Annex of the NDC for assumptions used for projected BAU and emission reduction (unconditional/CM1 and conditional/ CM2 reduction) for all sector categories (Energy, Waste, IPPU, Agriculture, and Forestry)","document_slug":"first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"\u003cp\u003e\"Assumptions used for baseline projection and policy scenarios for the 2020 to 2030 period are:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eLong-term economic growth will still be influenced by land use governance, tenurial issues, energy consumption, and quality of infrastructure connecting the archipelago.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eBesides GDP per capita, population growth, energy intensity and value added, the increasing demand of both domestic and international market on natural resources based commodities influence the dynamic behavior of each sector and the economy.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ePolicy scenario for post 2020 in the energy sector refers to Electricity Supply Business Plan (RUPTL) 2015-2024 and National Energy Policy (KEN).\"\u003c/li\u003e","document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648515,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"Baseline scenario targets: For dynamic baseline scenario targets, under what conditions will the baseline be recalculated","slug":"method_baseline_dynamic_recalculation","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64341,64344],"labels":{},"locations":{"IDN":[{"value":"Not Specified","document_slug":"revised_first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified","document_slug":"first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified","document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648516,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"Assumptions and methodological approaches for GHG reduction targets relative to emissions intensity","slug":"method_intensity","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64341,64344],"labels":{},"locations":{"IDN":[{"value":"Not Applicable","document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648517,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"Assumptions and methodological approaches for NDCs that include actions","slug":"method_actions","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64341,64344],"labels":{},"locations":{"IDN":[{"value":"Not Applicable","document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648518,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"Planned use of international market mechanisms","slug":"method_imm","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64341,64344,64325],"labels":{"1283678":{"name":"Yes / Possible","slug":null,"index":1},"1283679":{"name":"No","slug":null,"index":2},"1283680":{"name":"Not Specified","slug":null,"index":3},"1283681":{"name":"No Document Submitted","slug":null,"index":-2}},"locations":{"IDN":[{"value":"\"Presidential Regulation No. 110 Year 2025 provides guidance on NDC implementation and allows mobilization of finance from both domestic and international sources, including the use of Article 5 and Article 6 of the Paris Agreement to support NDC target achievement. Furthermore, in the effort of ensuring environmental integrity of both compliant and voluntary markets and its national benefits as well as international commitment, Indonesia is in the process of inter-ministerial and multistakeholder consultations on Voluntarv Carbon Market (VCM).\"","label_id":1283678,"document_slug":"second_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"\"Furthermore, Indonesia welcomes bilateral, regional and international cooperation in the NDC implementation as recognised under Article 6 of the Paris Agreement, that facilitate and expedite technology development and transfer, payment for performance, technical cooperation, and access to financial resources to support Indonesia’s climate mitigation and adaptation efforts towards a climate resilient future.\"","label_id":1283678,"document_slug":"revised_first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Yes / Possible","label_id":1283678,"document_slug":"first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Possible","label_id":1283678,"document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648519,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"Treatment of land sector","slug":"method_land_treatment","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64341,64345],"labels":{},"locations":{"IDN":[{"value":"Included as part of the broader target","document_slug":"second_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Included as part of the broader target","document_slug":"revised_first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Included in the target","document_slug":"first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Included in the target","document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648520,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"Coverage of the land sector as compared to total net emissions from the land sector, as a percentage if known","slug":"method_land_coverage","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64341,64345],"labels":{},"locations":{"IDN":[{"value":"Not Specified","document_slug":"second_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified","document_slug":"revised_first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified","document_slug":"first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified","document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648521,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"Methods: Assumed land sector accounting approach","slug":"method_land_accounting_approach","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64341,64345,64325],"labels":{"1284653":{"name":"Activity-Based","slug":null,"index":1},"1284654":{"name":"Land-Based","slug":null,"index":2},"1284655":{"name":"Activity-Based and Land-Based","slug":null,"index":3},"1284656":{"name":"Not Applicable","slug":null,"index":4},"1284657":{"name":"Not Specified","slug":null,"index":5},"1284658":{"name":"No Document Submitted","slug":null,"index":-2}},"locations":{"IDN":[{"value":"Not Specified","label_id":1284657,"document_slug":"second_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified","label_id":1284657,"document_slug":"revised_first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified","label_id":1284657,"document_slug":"first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified","label_id":1284657,"document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648522,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"Methods: Assumed land sector accounting method","slug":"method_land_accounting_method","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64341,64345,64325],"labels":{"1284659":{"name":"Forward-Looking Baseline","slug":null,"index":1},"1284660":{"name":"Gross-Net","slug":null,"index":2},"1284661":{"name":"Net-Net","slug":null,"index":3},"1284662":{"name":"Gross-Net and Net-Net","slug":null,"index":4},"1284663":{"name":"Not Applicable","slug":null,"index":5},"1284664":{"name":"Not Specified","slug":null,"index":6},"1284665":{"name":"No Document Submitted","slug":null,"index":-2}},"locations":{"IDN":[{"value":"Not Specified","label_id":1284664,"document_slug":"second_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified","label_id":1284664,"document_slug":"revised_first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified; however Indonesia communicates in NDC that \"Dashboard AFOLU\" is used for estimating emission from land-based sector","label_id":1284664,"document_slug":"first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified","label_id":1284664,"document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648523,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"Level against which emissions and removals from the land sector are accounted, including policy assumptions and methodologies employed","slug":"method_land_level","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64341,64345],"labels":{},"locations":{"IDN":[{"value":"Not Specified","document_slug":"second_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"\"The First Forest Reference Emission Level (FREL) for REDD+ was submitted to the UNFCCC Secretariat in December 2015, covering deforestation and forest degradation and peat decomposition. The FREL was set at 0.568 GtCO2-eq yr.-1 (AGB), using reference period of 1990-2012 and is used as the benchmark against actual emission starting from 2013 to 2020. These figures should be used as benchmark for evaluating REDD+ performance during the implementation period (up to 2020).The 2 nd FREL was submitted in January 2022 with significant improvements in a number of elements, including reference period, scope of activities, carbon pools, emission factor and method to calculate uncertainty. Currently the 2nd FREL is under assessment process by UNFCCC.\"","document_slug":"revised_first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified","document_slug":"first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified","document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648524,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"Any assumed use of methodologies to quantify and account for natural disturbances and legacy effects","slug":"method_land_method","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64341,64345],"labels":{},"locations":{"IDN":[{"value":"Not Specified","document_slug":"second_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified","document_slug":"revised_first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified","document_slug":"first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Not Specified","document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648525,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"Any ot